    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Added paper on datacenter traffic control review]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/papers-we-love/papers-we-love/pull/508</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/papers-we-love/papers-we-love/pull/508"/>
        <updated>2018-02-02T13:42:33.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h2 dir="auto">Paper Title: Datacenter Traffic Control: Understanding Techniques and Trade-offs</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Paper Year: 2017</h3>
<h3 dir="auto">Reasons for including paper</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>This paper covers a wide range of topics regarding how traffic is routed and scheduled across datacenter networks.</li>
<li>It also provides a short background on specifics of datacenter topology, traffic and management.</li>
<li>What makes this paper different is that it discusses trade-offs across many existing research proposals which allows readers to get familiar with important factors and considerations.</li>
<li>It is also rather conceptual and does not focus on detailed technical parameters which makes it an easy tutorial to datacenter traffic control.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
